## TIER — TIER 2, argued (the drafter's reading; Tuesday confirms at stamp)
**Tiers:** full weight (TIER 1) for security surfaces, data destruction, deploys and human handovers; through-code only for tests/docs/config/already-gated follow-ups. This gate is **TIER 2: through code** (red-proof, cells read against the ticket, full verify, CodeQL read, gitleaks) with no image legs.
**The case FOR tier 1:** RD-476 changes the text that steers every answer the assistant gives to every customer, and RD-857 adds a classifier (a guard that decides whether a capture is a user) whose false verdicts change which handler answers; `backend/server.js` is the shared file with gate 25's TIER-1 members; merging to main can deploy the demo if `CI_DEPLOY_ENABLED` were ever set (its repo value read `unset` at drafting — r10).
**Why that loses — TIER 2 (Tuesday's rulings, quoted):** ANSWER-6: *"RD-476 is tier 2 (customer-facing words; no security surface, no route or page change). Tuesday gates it through code. It will be batched with the next NexusAI gate"*; ANSWER-8: *"tier 2 (routing only, no answer text changed, no security surface)"* for RD-856; ANSWER-9: *"This is a routing fix inside Tuesday's authority"* for RD-857. No credential, no data-destroying path, no deploy recipe, no handover. **What keeps it from being a shrug:** the words were Kam's to approve and they are approved (cards `nexusai-rd476-assistant-prompt-words-1018` = b, then `nexusai-rd476-two-wording-fixes-1018` = a), so the gate's job on RD-476 is to prove the shipped text IS the approved text and nothing else (r2), and the interaction rows (r1, r9, r10) are where the batch can still be wrong. **A tier-2 verdict whose r2 (wording equality), r5-r7 (red proofs) or r8 (full verify) did not run is PROVISIONAL** (ruling (o) EXTENDED).

