**Read gate 22's §3a WHOLE at `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/qa-agent/briefs/2026-10-13_nexusai-gate-batch22.md`, gate 23's at `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/qa-agent/briefs/2026-10-16_nexusai-gate-batch23.md`, gate 24's at `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/qa-agent/briefs/2026-10-17_nexusai-gate24-rd848.md`, gate 25's at `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/qa-agent/briefs/2026-10-18_nexusai-gate25-rd761-rd794-merged.md` and gate 26's at `/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/TUESDAY/2_Project_Files/fleet/qa-agent/briefs/2026-10-18_nexusai-gate26-c170-be0fe37-merged.md`, and apply every rule** (their member-specific, docker, az, socket-ledger and package-build examples do not apply: this gate has no image legs and no outbound-path change). Restated where they bind:
- **H-1.** The ONLY permitted SESSION_SECRET printer, verbatim:
  `if [ -n "${SESSION_SECRET+x}" ]; then echo "SESSION_SECRET SET (length ${#SESSION_SECRET})"; else echo "SESSION_SECRET UNSET"; fi`.
  **FORBIDDEN:** `${SESSION_SECRET-…}`, `${SESSION_SECRET:-…}`, `${SESSION_SECRET+$SESSION_SECRET}`, `echo $SESSION_SECRET`, `printenv`, `env | grep`, `set | grep`, an echoed env array. Self-test the printer and gate 26's scan (`qa-h1-scan26.py`, `qa-h1-selftest26.sh`) before the first hold (the scan's control plants a DIFFERENT marker); never copy any `.throwaway-ss`.
- **H-3** a LANDING CONTROL for every hook, plant, mutant and probe (the value present in the data file the server reads AND echoed back by the reader route, never assumed). **H-4** the heartbeat is a **separate child**, the hold aborted if no HB **within 90 s** of the grant, the **max gap** reported (≤ 120 s). **H-6** every path quoted (`!CODING`, `Testing Agent MAIN`); every host jest run but the full verifies, every driver and every booted server under `qa-netbelt.sb` / `qa-netbelt-nodns.sb` (by copy) with its landing control. **H-7/H-8** mutants by a quoted tool (`qa-applymut.py` in gate 25's `inst/`, or `qa-mut24.py`) with a negative control; landed = "the exact mutated text is present AND the original text is absent once the new text is removed"; **an edit whose anchor is absent FAILS LOUDLY and nothing downstream runs on that tree.** **H-9** byte plants by `Buffer`, checked by `xxd -l 16` and `wc -c`, never `echo`/`printf`/heredoc/`JSON.stringify`. **H-11/H-18** `/bin/bash` explicitly, `"${sha}:${path}"` (zsh eats `:s`/`:a`; a bare `=====` line is a zsh error). **H-14** every driver ends `END ok` or `END VOID <reason>`. **H-17** absolute tool paths; assert each arm STARTED (jest's first suite, the listen line); censuses by `pgrep`, never `/bin/ps`. **H-20 (deadlines, `qa-to.sh`, rc 142 = fired):** targeted cells 600 s, each full verify 2,400 s, each c57 runner invocation 5,400 s, offline npm ci 600 s, each server boot + probe set 300 s. **H-21** every mutated file restored by a `trap … EXIT` (INT, TERM) installed BEFORE the first mutation, hash-compared to its pin (`model-config.js` head blob, `backend/server.js` head blob — read at start). **H-22** never nest `sandbox-exec` (it exits 71). **H-24** jest ARRAY options after the paths; lists built in bash. **H-26** ls-remote retried 5 × ~10 s on `Permission denied (publickey)`; a failure is UNKNOWN. **H-27** THE MODEL RULE. **H-29** the seats' and other gates' evidence is METHOD only. **H-31** offline host node