## 3b. THE NEGATIVE-ASSERTION SWEEP (C-102) — scoped to this batch
**Two changes can disarm a cell without touching it: A edits a shared preload and the ledger's row shape; B/C change which handler answers a whole family of "who/what/how much has …" questions, and the OLD substring behaviour may have been relied on by a cell for its green.** (1) Enumerate every cell that (a) requires `rd395-llm-mock-preload` or `rd395-server-harness` and reads the ledger, or (b) POSTs `/api/chat` with a lookup-shaped question, or (c) names `commonWords`, the not-found text or `checkForCurrentUserQuery`. (2) For each: does it still reach the line it is NAMED for on V3? A cell whose green now comes from a different path than the one it names is DISARMED — name it. (3) Self-test first or ABORT (a positive control, a negative control, a non-empty population). (4) Report population, negative cells, still reaching, disarmed.

