## 9. Floor discipline — MERGES GO FIRST, the jest lock, THE DEADLINE RULE
1. **MERGES GO FIRST (ruling i) — NO BY-HAND YIELD.** The jest lock `session-tools/nexusai-lock.sh` (`jest <tag> [--replace <own-ticket>] <cmd…>`) on the Laptop-DEV base (ruling q) is shared with S101O and gate 27. **Do ALL lock-free work first** (pins, hashes, reads, r0, r1, r2, r7, r11, r12, r13, the offline npm ci, the self-tests). **Then file your holds ONE AT A TIME**, tagged `qa-g28-…`, each a tracked child; a ticket queued AHEAD of you is waited behind (FIFO); at a wait deadline, `--replace`; **once granted, carry on.** **QUEUE, NEVER TAKE OVER:** never kill, signal, move or edit another seat's process, lock, owner file, ticket or worktree.
2. **Hold a lock for a planned block of work, never idle (H-28).**
3. **Count foreign servers and seats the C-125 way, anchored on YOUR OWN claude pid; the NEGATIVE controls (all must classify FOREIGN in the same run) are the claude pids the launcher DERIVED LIVE — the coordinator pane, every live `Datasec/NexusAI-*` pane, `fleet-monitor` if a claude runs under it, every live peer `QA/*` pane — listed at the end of your prompt.** Re-read them at every hold's start; **a hold with NO live negative control aborts.** Reuse `qa-floorlib26.sh` BY COPY with YOUR pid as `ROOT` and these as `NEG`, and `qa-floorcount.py`. Record the foreign server count beside every result.
4. **A zero is reportable only beside a control that fired in the same window** — "LOST 0" (the names tool's planted missing id), "0 unexplained prompt lines" (r2's planted word), "0 new alerts" (r7's PR #58 read), "0 new leaks" (r11's planted string), "0 flips outside the named" (r6's old-vs-old and reproduced RD-856 flip).
5. **THE LOAD RULE (ruling p):** start a hold and any full jest only below a 1-minute load of **8**; record `uptime` beside every hold's start.

**6. THE DEADLINE RULE** — every step has a written DEADLINE (H-20), a HEARTBEAT line at least every **2 minutes** in a hold, a step silent for **5 minutes** is aborted and reported, every child is killed in a `finally` by pid from your own ancestry, never by pattern (C-174); every booted server is stopped by its own pid and its port read free afterwards.

